<.shell title="Overview" current={:index}>
  <h1>Style guide (draft)</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    GOV.UK's patterns and plain look, Carbon's dense tables, in light and dark. Standalone: none
    of this reaches the app. <a href="/styles">The current style guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Palette</h2>
  <p>
    Every color is a token with a light and a dark value. Components use tokens only, so dark
    mode is a swap, not a second set of styles. The switch in the top bar picks the mode for
    the page; both are shown here side by side.
  </p>
  <div class="modes">
    <div
      :for={{mode, label} <- [{"theme-light", "Light"}, {"theme-dark", "Dark"}]}
      class={["mode", mode]}
    >
      <h3>{label}</h3>
      <div :for={{group, tokens} <- palette()}>
        <h4>{group}</h4>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div :for={{name, light, dark, use} <- tokens} class="swatch" title={use}>
            <div class="chipcolor" style={"background: var(--#{name})"}></div>
            <strong>{name}</strong>
            <span>{if mode == "theme-light", do: light, else: dark}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-card">
        <p>
          Body text with <a href="#">a link</a> and <span class="muted">muted text</span>.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button class="btn">Primary</button>
          <button class="btn secondary">Secondary</button>
          <span class="tag success">Active</span>
          <span class="tag incident">Incident</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Typography</h2>
  <p>
    IBM Plex Sans, with tabular figures everywhere so numbers line up. 16px body, 14px in
    tables.
  </p>
  <h1>Heading 1, 32px</h1>
  <h2 style="margin-top: 0">Heading 2, 24px</h2>
  <h3 style="margin-top: 0">Heading 3, 19px</h3>
  <p class="lead">Lead text introduces a page in one or two sentences.</p>
  <p>
    Body text. Search and rescue team managers read this between calls, so it stays short and
    plain. Hours like <strong>212h 30m</strong> and <strong>18h 05m</strong> line up because
    figures are tabular.
  </p>
  <p class="muted small">Small muted text, for captions and table notes.</p>

  <h2>Buttons</h2>
  <p>Flat, with a hard bottom edge. One primary action per page.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <button class="btn">Save and continue</button>
    <button class="btn secondary">Cancel</button>
    <button class="btn success">Create letter</button>
    <button class="btn danger">Delete clause</button>
    <button class="btn ghost">More information</button>
    <button class="btn" disabled>Disabled</button>
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <button class="btn sm">Small</button>
    <button class="btn sm secondary">Small secondary</button>
    <button class="btn sm success">Create letter</button>
    <button class="btn sm danger">Remove</button>
  </div>

  <h2>Tags</h2>
  <div class="actions">
    <span class="tag">Default</span>
    <span class="tag primary">Primary</span>
    <span class="tag success">Qualified</span>
    <span class="tag warning">Expires in 12 days</span>
    <span class="tag danger">Not invited</span>
    <span class="tag info">Synced</span>
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <span class="tag incident">Incident</span>
    <span class="tag exercise">Exercise</span>
    <span class="tag event">Event</span>
  </div>

  <h2>Messages</h2>
  <div class="banner success" role="status">
    <div class="banner-title">Success</div>
    <div class="banner-body">
      <p><strong>4 attendance changes were saved to D4H.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="banner" role="region" aria-label="Important">
    <div class="banner-title">Important</div>
    <div class="banner-body">
      <p>D4H refreshes every night at 2am. Changes made in D4H today show up tomorrow.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="warning-text">
    <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
    <span>Attendance can't be changed once the activity is published in D4H.</span>
  </div>
  <div class="inset">
    Members are matched by name, email, or phone. You review every change before it's made.
  </div>

  <h2>Focus</h2>
  <p>
    Press Tab on this page. Everything you can reach gets the GOV.UK yellow focus, the same in
    both modes: <a href="#">a link</a>, <button class="btn sm">a button</button>, and inputs on
    the forms page.
  </p>
</.shell>
